WEBVTT

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.250
- We've got you.
- Thank you.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.333
Come on, let's get out of here.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.208
- Not so fast.
- No!

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:37.000
Come on, hand over the bear.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.333
No. We won't do that.

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:42.583
Mrs Brown?

00:00:43.417 --> 00:00:45.542
- He's family.
- Family?

00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:47.750
You're not even the same species.

00:00:48.542 --> 00:00:50.417
It's true.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.542
It is true.

00:00:52.625 --> 00:00:55.917
And when I first met Paddington,
I wanted nothing to do with him.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.792
But my wonderful wife,
she opened her heart to him

00:01:00.875 --> 00:01:03.417
and so did my incredible children.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.500
- And now I have, too.
- Henry...

00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:08.708
it doesn't matter that he comes
from the other side of the world

00:01:08.833 --> 00:01:11.042
or that he's a different species

00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:13.792
or that he has
a worrying marmalade habit.

00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:17.875
We love Paddington.
And that makes him family!

00:01:17.958 --> 00:01:20.208
And families stick together!

00:01:20.292 --> 00:01:24.750
So if you want him,
you'll have to take us all!

00:01:24.792 --> 00:01:26.042
OK, then.

00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:28.333
When I say "all"...

00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:30.250
- I've never stuffed a human, but...
- Wait.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:32.750
Wait!

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:36.250
- You don't need to do that.
- Paddington!

00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:38.125
- No!
- Yes.

00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:40.458
That's right. Come, come.

00:01:46.792 --> 00:01:50.083
Erm, could I have one last request?

00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:52.333
What is it?

00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:55.208
I'd like a sandwich.
There's one in my hat.

00:01:56.042 --> 00:01:57.125
Go on, then.

00:01:58.208 --> 00:01:59.500
Thank you.

00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:14.500
Whoa!

00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:15.875
Who-o-oa!

00:02:18.792 --> 00:02:20.833
Nice try, bear!

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.500
The crew's nest!

00:02:26.542 --> 00:02:28.083
Mrs. Bird.

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.375
What?

00:02:29.458 --> 00:02:32.667
Hey, why didn't you look
where you were going?

00:02:32.708 --> 00:02:34.792
Ah, shut your piehole.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.000
- Mrs Bird, you saved me.
- Oh!

00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:42.292
- Paddington!
- A bear.

00:02:43.625 --> 00:02:46.917
Go easy. I have a dreadful headache.

00:03:06.792 --> 00:03:08.000
Hello?

00:03:08.083 --> 00:03:10.417
- Hi, Dad.
- Hello, Mr Brown.

00:03:10.917 --> 00:03:12.667
- Hello.
- What's going on?

00:03:12.708 --> 00:03:16.875
What a lovely surprise.
I didn't expect you home so early.

00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:21.792
- Something special's going on.
- More sugar.

00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:24.708
- Look at this. Hello, everyone.
- Hi, Dad.

00:03:24.792 --> 00:03:27.625
- Hi, big fella. What's cooking?
- Marmalade, Mr Brown.

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:30.125
- Go on, have a taste.
- Hmm, delicious.

00:03:30.208 --> 00:03:32.958
Just one sandwich contains
all the vitamins and minerals

00:03:33.083 --> 00:03:34.583
a bear needs for the whole day.

00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:37.000
So does that mean
I don't have to eat vegetables?

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.458
- He said "bear", not "boy".
- Sorry, Jonathan.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.125
- Thank you, Judy.
- Judy.

00:03:41.208 --> 00:03:44.833
Now, has anyone seen...
Ah, thank you, Mrs Bird.

00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:47.125
I think every home
should have a marmalade day.

00:03:47.208 --> 00:03:49.917
- And a bear.
- Especially a bear.

00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:52.417
Home.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.250
Dear Aunt Lucy.

00:03:57.333 --> 00:04:00.708
I'm sorry I haven't written sooner
but so much has been happening.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.792
I even met the explorer's daughter,

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:06.667
but she tried to stuff me,
so Mrs Bird threw her off a roof.

00:04:06.708 --> 00:04:07.833
Millicent Clyde...

00:04:07.917 --> 00:04:10.583
The judge didn't think
that prison would do her any good.

00:04:10.625 --> 00:04:12.792
So instead, he gave her
community service...

00:04:12.875 --> 00:04:15.417
No, please! Anything! Anything but that!

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.833
..In the petting zoo.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:23.042
- Get a move on, dung breath!
- It's not my breath!

00:04:26.917 --> 00:04:30.833
Back in Windsor Gardens,
life is very different.

00:04:30.917 --> 00:04:33.792
Mrs Bird says it's because
things are finally set fair

00:04:33.958 --> 00:04:37.250
and it's had a tremendous effect
on her knees.

00:04:37.333 --> 00:04:41.208
Judy's embarrassment is clearing up
and she's even let Mrs Brown meet Tony.

00:04:41.292 --> 00:04:43.458
- You can't say anything.
- Of course not.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.167
- You can't touch me.
- I won't touch anyone, darling.

00:04:46.292 --> 00:04:48.917
- And you're not gonna cry.
- No! No.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.542
There's just a lot going on
in my heart right now.

00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:53.958
We process things very differently,
you and I.

00:04:54.083 --> 00:04:55.750
- I know.
- Good.

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.000
Mum, this is Tony.

00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:01.667
- Welcome to the family.
- Oh. Mum!

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.667
Sorry. Sorry. Not crying.

00:05:06.375 --> 00:05:07.458
Henry?

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.250
I'm sorry about her.

00:05:10.875 --> 00:05:14.042
She's weird. Er, but we all are.

00:05:15.667 --> 00:05:18.125
Tea, anyone? No? No.

00:05:18.208 --> 00:05:21.833
And Mr Brown is helping
Jonathan build an enormous rocket.

00:05:21.917 --> 00:05:23.292
Are you sure about this, Dad?

00:05:23.417 --> 00:05:25.708
If we're gonna get
this bad boy into orbit,

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.833
we're gonna need
all the nitroglycerin.

00:05:27.917 --> 00:05:31.708
Although Jonathan worries about his
father's reckless attitude to safety.

00:05:31.792 --> 00:05:33.875
Houston, we may have a problem.

00:05:33.958 --> 00:05:35.167
Duck!

00:05:39.542 --> 00:05:43.375
Mrs Brown says that
in London, everyone is different,

00:05:43.458 --> 00:05:46.542
but that means anyone can fit in.

00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:48.208
I think she must be right,

00:05:48.292 --> 00:05:52.500
because although I don't look like
anyone else, I really do feel at home.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:57.208
I will never be like other people,
but that's alright.

00:05:57.292 --> 00:05:58.958
Because I am a bear.

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:01.875
A bear called Paddington.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.458
Come on, Paddington!

00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:08.417
♪ I had to laugh
till I couldn't laugh no more

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.875
♪ Like an old Chinaman out on the ﬂoor

00:06:10.958 --> 00:06:13.625
♪ Pass me by, hopping like a clown

00:06:13.708 --> 00:06:16.375
♪ I told meself
that he rarely go into town

00:06:16.458 --> 00:06:18.917
♪ And there was also a rajah gentleman

00:06:19.042 --> 00:06:21.708
♪ Americans and British, West Indians

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.583
♪ Tell you one thing
that really amused me

00:06:24.708 --> 00:06:26.708
♪ Believe it or not
was a pretty Japanese

00:06:27.042 --> 00:06:28.292
♪ And they were singing

00:06:28.375 --> 00:06:30.667
♪ Ju-ba, ju-ba, a-ju-Ii-ba

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:33.083
♪ They're jumping here
and they're jumping there

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:35.875
♪ With a boolah boolah boolah boolah
boolah boolah-ea

00:06:35.958 --> 00:06:38.000
♪ The people going crazy

00:06:38.083 --> 00:06:39.375
Ooh!

